From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:02:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/metal: Don't wait forever for a hidden window's drawable
 or present.

Core Animation gives no drawable to a window that is hidden or
occluded until it shows again, and it never reports such a window's
frames as presented. With an infinite timeout, acquire spun until the
window showed again and vkWaitForPresentKHR waited for good: a game
started in the background (Age of Empires II: Definitive Edition,
through DXVK) hung in its first frame.

After Core Animation's own 1 s wait for a drawable, an acquire with an
infinite timeout now reports VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR, so the
application recreates the swapchain or drops the frame. A present wait
longer than 100 ms counts the frame as presented after 100 ms, which a
visible window always reaches within a refresh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
index 54542c6..0d9c8f8 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
@@ -620,6 +620,12 @@ wsi_metal_swapchain_acquire_next_image(struct wsi_swapchain *wsi_chain,
          return VK_SUCCESS;
       }
 
+      /* No drawable within Core Animation's 1 s: the window is hidden or occluded, and Core Animation holds the
+       * drawables it was given. Don't spin until the window shows again (an infinite timeout hung the caller):
+       * report the swapchain out of date, so the application recreates it or drops the frame. */
+      if (info->timeout == UINT64_MAX)
+         return VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR;
+
       /* Check for timeout. */
       struct timespec current_time;
       clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &current_time);
@@ -732,6 +738,13 @@ wsi_metal_swapchain_wait_for_present(struct wsi_swapchain *wsi_chain,
 
    struct timespec abs_timespec;
    uint64_t abs_timeout = 0;
+   /* A hidden or occluded window never shows its frames, and the presented handler may then never run:
+    * a long wait counts the frame as presented after 100 ms (a visible window presents within a refresh). */
+   const uint64_t hidden_cap = 100 * 1000 * 1000ull;
+   const bool capped = timeout > hidden_cap;
+
+   if (capped)
+      timeout = hidden_cap;
 
    if (timeout != 0)
       abs_timeout = os_time_get_absolute_timeout(timeout);
@@ -751,7 +764,7 @@ wsi_metal_swapchain_wait_for_present(struct wsi_swapchain *wsi_chain,
                                           &present_info->mutex,
                                           &abs_timespec);
       if (ret == thrd_timedout) {
-         result = VK_TIMEOUT;
+         result = capped ? VK_SUCCESS : VK_TIMEOUT;
          break;
       }
       if (ret != thrd_success) {
